{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ועבדתם את ה' אלהיכם", :translit "va'avadetem et H' elokeichem", :gloss "and you (pl.) shall serve YHWH your Elohim"} {:he "וברך את לחמך", :translit "u'veirach et lachmecha", :gloss "and He will bless your (sg.) bread"} {:he "תפלת רבים שאינה נמאסת", :translit "tefilat rabbim she'einah nema'esset", :gloss "the prayer of the many is not rejected"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between plural ועבדתם and singular וברך to derive two distinct lessons"}], :frame {:text "The principle that the prayer of the many is not rejected appears in tractate Berakhot 8a, where R. Yochanan states that one should always join the congregation since the prayer of the many is not rejected.", :sources ["Berakhot 8a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וברך", :translit "u'veirach", :gloss "and He will bless"} {:he "וברך פרי בטנך", :translit "u'veirach pri vitnecha", :gloss "and He will bless the fruit of your womb"} {:he "וברך עלי את אלקנה ואת אשתו", :translit "u'veirach ali et elkanah ve'et ishto", :gloss "and he blessed Elkanah and his wife"} {:he "וברך את לחמך ואת מימיך", :translit "u'veirach et lachmecha ve'et meimecha", :gloss "and He will bless your bread and your water"} {:he "כי היכי דתתברך פרי בטנה", :translit "kei haikei dititbareich pri vitnah", :gloss "so that the fruit of her womb be blessed"} {:he "פרי בטנה", :translit "pri vitnah", :gloss "the fruit of her womb"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וברך" "וברך פרי בטנך" "וברך עלי את אלקנה ואת אשתו"]}], :frame {:text "The practice of sending the cup of blessing to one's household is discussed in tractate Berakhot 51a. The verse וברך עלי את אלקנה appears in 1 Samuel 2:20, where Eli blesses Elkanah and his wife Hannah, after which she conceives.", :sources ["Berakhot 51a" "1 Samuel 2:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מימיך", :translit "meimecha", :gloss "your waters"} {:he "ואם מימיך נשתה וגו'", :translit "ve'im meimecha nishteh vegomer", :gloss "and if you drink from